            <ArticleTitle>Inhaler devices for asthma and COPD: choice and technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>641-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nurses caring for patients with asthma or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease need a good basic knowledge of the types of inhaler devices available and which may suit, for example, a very young child, an active young person or an elderly patient with dexterity problems. This Study describes the advantages and disadvantages of some commonly prescribed devices.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
